      "concept": "Notice record retention with timestamp and content integrity",
      "legalIntent": "Ensure operators retain complete notice records for the required duration, preserving both the notice text content (including limiting language) and the associated receipt timestamp to enable verification of retention periods and record completeness.",
      "applicabilityGuidance": "Applies to software systems operated by entities offering the notice service to the public. The system must handle notice records (stored notices with receipt timestamps). Excludes private household use. Excludes temporary test records from the retention requirement.",
      "criteria": [
        {
          "statement": "Each non-temporary-test notice record must be retained for at least 7 days from its receipt timestamp.",
          "criterionId": "C-1"
        },
        {
          "statement": "Each retained record must include both the notice text and its associated receipt timestamp.",
          "criterionId": "C-2"
        },
        {
          "statement": "The notice text must be preserved without removing its limiting language.",
          "criterionId": "C-3"
        },
        {
          "statement": "The receipt timestamp is recorded when the notice is received, not when it is drafted.",
          "criterionId": "C-4"
        }
